 "notes": "Thick blue curve of Fig. 3b (95% CL upper limit on Lambda_gamma^-1 vs m_phi), extracted pixel-wise from the embedded 3087x3233 raster in figures/results_combined.pdf. Axis calibration from major ticks (x: 1e-20/1e-15/1e-10 eV at px 405.5/1377.5/2350; y: 69.1 px/decade, bottom frame=1e-25 GeV^-1), cross-checked by the curve endpoints landing exactly on the 10 Hz - 5 kHz search band (4.1e-14 to 2.1e-11 eV). Converted via d_e = M_Pl/(sqrt(4pi) Lambda_gamma) = 3.44e18 GeV x Lambda_gamma^-1, the paper's own definition matching the Damour-Donoghue convention. The likelihood bounds mu=(1/Lambda_gamma + 1/Lambda_e); the quoted limit applies to either coupling with the other set to zero, so the Lambda_e^-1 (d_me) curve in Fig. 3a is numerically identical (verified: panels agree to <0.03 dex). Paper notes the plotted curve was smoothed for visual purposes. rho_local = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed.",
